# Store upload credentials for the fastlane lanes.
#
# Copy this file to fastlane/.env and fill in the values. fastlane loads
# fastlane/.env automatically; it is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
#     cp fastlane/.env.example fastlane/.env
#     bundle exec fastlane doctor
#
# Deliberately NOT in the repository-root .env: that file is the pre-release
# provider contract, and scripts/verify-prerelease-env.mjs requires every key in
# it to hold a value in .env.local. Adding store credentials there would make
# `make prerelease-preflight` demand an App Store key before a provider matrix
# run, which has nothing to do with uploading a listing.
#
# Both secrets live outside the repository. Keep them out of any bundle: native
# Release bundling sets EXPO_NO_DOTENV=1 for exactly this reason.

# --- App Store Connect ------------------------------------------------------
# App Store Connect -> Users and Access -> Integrations -> App Store Connect API
# Generate a key with the App Manager role. The .p8 downloads once and cannot be
# retrieved again; store it outside this repository.
APP_STORE_CONNECT_API_KEY_ID=
APP_STORE_CONNECT_API_ISSUER_ID=
APP_STORE_CONNECT_API_KEY_PATH=/Users/you/.appstoreconnect/private_keys/AuthKey_XXXXXXXXXX.p8

# --- Google Play ------------------------------------------------------------
# There is no "API access" page in Play Console and no Google Cloud project to
# link. Both were removed; older guides still describe them, and Play Console's
# Settings genuinely has no such entry. Two steps, two consoles:
#
# Google Cloud console (any project)
#   1. IAM and admin -> Service accounts -> Create service account. Skip the
#      optional Cloud role grants; Play access is not granted here.
#   2. Open the account -> Keys -> Add key -> Create new key -> JSON. It
#      downloads once. Put it outside this repository and point at it below.
#   3. APIs and services -> Library -> enable "Google Play Android Developer
#      API" on that project. Check this first if authentication fails.
#
# Play Console -> Users and permissions -> Invite new users
#   Paste the service-account address (name@project-id.iam.gserviceaccount.com).
#   For this app grant "Manage store presence" for listing text and graphics,
#   and "Release to production, exclude devices, and use Play App Signing" for
#   the release lane. Service-account invitations apply immediately, but new
#   grants can take a few minutes to propagate.
#
# Confirm with: bundle exec fastlane doctor online:true
SUPPLY_JSON_KEY=/Users/you/.playconsole/mrbroccoli-service-account.json

# --- Optional ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed if a lane falls back to Apple ID authentication instead of the
# API key. The API key is preferred: it does not prompt for two-factor codes.
APPLE_ID=
APPLE_TEAM_ID=
